# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so checked-out files get CRLF endings.
# That is fine for source, but FATAL for a shell script: `#!/bin/sh\r` makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter literally named "sh\r" and the hook dies with a
# "bad interpreter" error — on a fresh clone, silently, at the worst moment.
.githooks/** text eol=lf
